#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# bins

#% text
# `bins` is an option of `histogram`: `bins: n` uses about `n` bins of a round width, `bins: [w]` bins of width `w`, `bins: [lo, hi, w]` bins of width `w` from `lo` to `hi`, and `automatic` a choice from the data.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The bins are half-open intervals `[a, a + w)`; data outside `[lo, hi]` is left out.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
seed(1); data = random_real([0, 1], 200); histogram(data, bins: 5)
#% output
#= image("bins.files/bins-1.svgz")

#% cell
histogram(data, bins: [0.05])
#% output
#= image("bins.files/bins-2.svgz")

#% cell
histogram(data, bins: [0, 2, 0.25])
#% output
#= image("bins.files/bins-3.svgz")

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A normal sample with the automatic choice:

#% cell
seed(2); histogram(random_variate(normal_distribution(0, 1), 500), bins: automatic)
#% output
#= image("bins.files/bins-4.svgz")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `histogram`, `normalized`
